0300: guest physical memory ranges (City Folk; generic, superset of SMS 0101)

GXSetAuroraPhysicalMemoryRange(physStart, size, host) registers up to 4 windows for console
physical addresses (Wii: MEM1 at 0, MEM2 at 0x10000000); GXSetAuroraPhysicalMemory(base, mask)
is SMS's call (one window at 0). With a window registered, raw writes from game code are
resolved: CP vertex array bases (0xA0-0xAF), BP TX_SETIMAGE3 (24-bit address field for MEM2),
TLUT loads (BP 0x64/0x65) and TMEM TLUT references, and GX_CMD_CALL_DL (opcode 0x40), whose
list is processed in place (a call inside a called list is ignored, as on the hardware).
NW4R g3d's shape display lists set their vertex arrays this way and EGG calls lists from the
FIFO: without it every g3d model is invisible.

diff --git a/include/dolphin/gx/GXAurora.h b/include/dolphin/gx/GXAurora.h
index 8ec5b00..20335be 100644
--- a/include/dolphin/gx/GXAurora.h
+++ b/include/dolphin/gx/GXAurora.h
@@ -236,6 +236,20 @@ u32 GXGetAuroraAccuracy();
 #define GX_AURORA_TEXGEN_BEYOND_TEXCOORD0 2
 void GXSetAuroraTexGenBeyondCount(u32 mode);
 
+/*
+ * Guest physical memory (recompiled/emulated games; 0300, a superset of SMS's 0101). Display lists
+ * and raw FIFO writes from game code carry console physical addresses: CP vertex array bases
+ * (0xA0-0xAF), BP texture image addresses (TX_SETIMAGE3), TLUT load addresses (BP 0x64), TMEM
+ * TLUT references, and display list calls (GX_CMD_CALL_DL, opcode 0x40). Each registered range
+ * maps physical [start, start + size) to host memory at `host` (up to 4 ranges, e.g. the Wii's
+ * MEM1 at 0 and MEM2 at 0x10000000; GameCube: one range at 0). With a range registered, Aurora
+ * resolves such writes (GXLoadTexObj/GXLoadTlut metadata still takes precedence when present);
+ * without one (default) they are ignored as before. Addresses outside every range are ignored.
+ * GXSetAuroraPhysicalMemory(base, mask) = one range at 0 of size mask + 1 (SMS's call).
+ */
+void GXSetAuroraPhysicalMemoryRange(u32 physStart, u32 size, void* host);
+void GXSetAuroraPhysicalMemory(void* base, u32 mask);
+
 /*
  * Debug marker stuff
  */
diff --git a/lib/dolphin/gx/GXAurora.cpp b/lib/dolphin/gx/GXAurora.cpp
index d4a8960..7dce6bd 100644
--- a/lib/dolphin/gx/GXAurora.cpp
+++ b/lib/dolphin/gx/GXAurora.cpp
@@ -79,6 +79,16 @@ void GXSetAuroraAccuracy(u32 flags) { aurora::gx::g_accuracyFlags.store(flags, s
 u32 GXGetAuroraAccuracy() { return aurora::gx::g_accuracyFlags.load(std::memory_order_relaxed); }
 
 void GXSetAuroraTexGenBeyondCount(u32 mode) { aurora::gx::g_texGenBeyondCount.store(mode, std::memory_order_relaxed); }
+void GXSetAuroraPhysicalMemoryRange(u32 physStart, u32 size, void* host) {
+  auto& ranges = aurora::gx::g_physRanges;
+  for (auto& r : ranges) {
+    if (r.size == 0 || r.start == physStart) {
+      r = {physStart, size, static_cast<u8*>(host)};
+      return;
+    }
+  }
+}
+void GXSetAuroraPhysicalMemory(void* base, u32 mask) { GXSetAuroraPhysicalMemoryRange(0, mask + 1, base); }
 
